          "id": "c1",
          "value": {
            "language": "en",
            "text": "The East Carolina University College of Business is the business school of East Carolina University, located in Greenville, North Carolina. The school originated in 1936 as the Department of Commerce, became the School of Business in 1960 and adopted the College of Business name in 2002. The Association to Advance Collegiate Schools of Business accredited its undergraduate programs in 1967 and its graduate programs in 1976.\n\nThe college offers undergraduate degrees in business administration and hospitality management and graduate degrees in business administration and accounting. It also offers a dual-degree opportunity with the Brody School of Medicine. Its history includes a move from the Rawl Building to the Harold H. Bate Building and the development of online MBA courses."
          },
          "verification": "supported"
        }
      ],
